gue you're  having that  now granny goodness started life off as  baby goodness i think i doubt she was a  granny  and she was seen as one of the peasants  of the planet however a dark side picked  her up out of poverty  and trained her to be one of his elite  soldiers a hilarious part in the  training was that she had to raise a dog  and at the end of it she was ordered to  kill it instead she killed the trainer  for ordering her to do that  and it just shows that she is quite a  ruthless person  now she did later turn around and kill a  dog for darkseid  and this showed loyalty to him and him  alone since then she's run orphanages in  search of warriors to join his ranks  and has been integral to the comics  though pretty funny to look at  don't make jokes about her unless you  want that crappy taste of joss whedon's  justice league in your throat  and he's definitely not one to mess with  and lastly i just want to discuss  jared leto's joker though i did an  initial reaction to this first look  i didn't really go into all the ins and  outs of it and i kind of want to touch  upon what snyder said  rather than just giving my personal  opinion this is linkedin with the  nightmare timeline  and though joker wasn't originally part  of it snyder said the following  when discussing the character the joker  is really the only thing that i thought  of in retrospect  but i will say that it was always my  intention to bring joker into that world  and i think with this being the story of  second chances it also makes sense to  bring  leto back as he's a phenomenal actor who  many feel was let down by dc  in suicide squad in the shots leto's  joker wears a bulletproof vest  that's adorned with police badges and  snyder says that these are his trophies  when discussing the scene itself the  director told vanity fair  the cool thing about the scene is that  it's joker talking directly to batman  about batman it's joker analyzing batman  about who he is  and what he is that's the thing i also  felt like fans deserved from the dc  universe  that is to say the giaraletto joker and  the ben affleck batman  they never really got together it seemed  uncool to me that we'd make it all the  way through this incarnation of batman  and joker  without seeing them come together right  now  over me he didn't say that but he did go  on to say the scene explains why bruce  had the joker card taped to his gun that  you see in batman versus superman  i'd always wanted to explore the death  of robin and if there was going to be an  x movie  which of course there probably won't be  i wanted to do a thing where in  flashbacks we learn how robin died  how joker killed him and burned down  wayne manor and that whole thing that  happened between he and bruce  so lots of things there that sound  absolutely amazing  and i would love to see the rumored ben  affleck hbo max batman show  explore not only the death of jason todd  but the destruction of a mana and more  there are really a lot of potential  avenues and i absolutely  love the trailer now obviously i'd love  to hear your thoughts on it so make sure  you comment below and let me know  and if you enjoyed this video then  please drop a thumbs up don't forget  that on the 28th of february we're  giving away three copies of the mcu  phase 3 4k box set to our subscribers  don't don't tell them i like the marvel  universe as well now all you have to do  to be on the chance of winning is like  the video  make sure you subscribe with  notifications on and drop a comment  below with your thoughts on the trailer  the winners of last month's competition  are on screen right now  so if that's you then message me on  twitter the links to our socials are in  the description  and you can also support the channel by  clicking the join button and as a thank  you you get videos like this early  if you want something else to watch then  make sure you check out our breakdown of  one division  which will be linked on screen right now  we went over the episode top to bottom  and pointed out a lot of the easter eggs  and gave our theories on what's  happening  so it's definitely worth checking out if  you want to know more by the way thank  you for sticking through the video  i've been paul i'll see you next time  take care peace  and enjoy valentine's day even though  you ruined it with this video  much love
 

